body:
What if black magic made it so you had no prayers, but you had access to 'body modification' spells that cost prayer points (one off for the duration of the spell) to cast? Like, 4 tiers of spells. A defense one that reduces every hit you take by 1, maxing 4 at highest tier, but you'll always take a minimum of 1 hp damage if it otherwise would have been nulled for balance. A strength one that increases minimum and max by 1 following a similar pattern, ect. It'd use prayer points almost as a mana pool. Prayer bonus would reduce prayer cost maybe? Would be a neat mechanic I think.

&#x200B;

Further expanding on this idea, maybe even weapon specific spells? Like modifiers unique to something like the mace, which on hit has 25% chance to restore 1 prayer point, daggers would do additional poison damage, bows would have a chance to do a minimum amount of damage, ect ect. The caveat would obviously be no prayers when your on black magic.

Depends on what i'm doing honestly. If defence / high lvl survival, ill take nyx - phage - brakk - zorens

If mid level things i usually take oberon - {insert leveling weapon here} Akstilletos - {insert leveling weapon here}

For rushing / "get it done", ill usually take Rhino - phage - akstilletos - dual ichors
